{"name":"Congress Blue","hex":"#02478e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"congress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A formal gathering or assembly of persons; a conference held to discuss or decide on a specific question.","A legislative body of a state, originally the bicameral legislature of the United States of America."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To assemble together.","To meet in a congress."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/congress"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Congress","blocks":[{"text":"A congress is a formal meeting of the representatives of different countries, constituent states, organizations, trade unions, political parties, or other groups. The term originated in Late Middle English to denote an encounter during battle, from the Latin congressus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Europa_Congres_Ridderzaal_Den_Haag._Overzicht%2C_Bestanddeelnr_902-7379.jpg/330px-Europa_Congres_Ridderzaal_Den_Haag._Overzicht%2C_Bestanddeelnr_902-7379.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Congress"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Buenos_Aires-Plaza_Congreso-Pensador_de_Rodin.jpg/500px-Buenos_Aires-Plaza_Congreso-Pensador_de_Rodin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Buenos_Aires-Plaza_Congreso-Pensador_de_Rodin.jpg/1280px-Buenos_Aires-Plaza_Congreso-Pensador_de_Rodin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Buenos_Aires-Plaza_Congreso-Pensador_de_Rodin.jpg/500px-Buenos_Aires-Plaza_Congreso-Pensador_de_Rodin.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Argentine National Congress in Buenos Aires","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABuenos_Aires-Plaza_Congreso-Pensador_de_Rodin.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Chess_congress%2C_Ormskirk.jpg/500px-Chess_congress%2C_Ormskirk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Chess_congress%2C_Ormskirk.jpg/500px-Chess_congress%2C_Ormskirk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chess congress","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChess_congress%2C_Ormskirk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2010._%D